From 3edff574a2a82a5b61c6d9f7da5cd26c65d7bd70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:17:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Kernels: other integrators of the non linear form added to
 the computations by kernels

When the non linear form contained other integrators than the one of
mfem-mgis (for instance a Robin boundary condition, given as a boundary
face integrator, or springs depending on the unknowns, given as a boundary
integrator), the residual and the tangent operator computed by kernels went
back to the loops of MFEM on all the elements: the residual was assembled
by mfem::NonlinearForm::Mult (the integrator of mfem-mgis giving null
contributions), and the stiffness matrices computed by kernels were stored
element by element and copied in the matrix by the element loop of MFEM.

The contributions of the domain, boundary and boundary face integrators
other than the integrator of mfem-mgis are now evaluated by loops copied
from mfem::NonlinearForm and restricted to them (markers of the attributes
included), on the host, and added respectively to the local vector of the
inner forces and to the local matrix assembled by kernels, before the
passage to the true degrees of freedom: the positions of the entries and
the global matrix with the pattern kept are used. On a GPU, the local
vector and the values of the local matrix are copied to the host at each
evaluation. The former path is kept for the forms with interior face
integrators or with an extension of MFEM.

The unknowns are prolongated on all the processes before the computations
which may fail on one process only, and a failure of the other integrators
is reported on all the processes. The numbers of evaluations of the
residual with the other integrators and of assemblies of the tangent
operator by kernels are given by getNumberOfOtherIntegratorsResidualEvaluations
and getNumberOfTangentOperatorAssembliesByKernels. The user guide
(batch_computations.rst, boundary_conditions.rst) is updated.

BatchIntegrationTest: springs as a boundary integrator, with or without
markers, as boundary face integrators with markers, as domain integrators
with markers on a mesh with two materials, and on an interior boundary
(boundary face integrator skipped, as by MFEM); a null integrator on the
interior faces (former path); numbers of evaluations of the residual with
the other integrators and of assemblies of the tangent operator by
kernels checked.
